coverage/
# Scoped with a leading slash on purpose — a real bug found while verifying
# this project's first `git init`: the old unscoped "storage/" matched ANY
# directory named "storage" anywhere under backend/, which silently included
# the real S3StorageProvider source at src/modules/profile/storage/ in the
# ignore list. This now only matches a top-level local runtime storage dir
# (leftover from the pre-S3 LocalDiskStorageProvider era, already deleted —
# docs/roadmap.md §3), which no longer exists on disk, kept only in case a
# local cache dir with this name is ever recreated.
/storage/
